Chapter: GuardPageWalk
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The genuine-allocation-walk arm of build/guard-page-test.ps1: no parked
 frontier and no substitution, unlike guard-page-probe.codex beside it. It
 lives in build/ for the sibling's other reason -- it never exits on a
 healthy tree (the guard halts it), so the battery's run-and-compare model
 cannot hold it.

 grow doubles a 64-char seed twelve times into a ~256 K-char text; walk then
 concatenates one character onto it per step, so every step is one real
 __str_concat of ~256 KB -- far under the 2 MB page, so the walk cannot step
 over the hole -- marching the frontier from the heap base into the guard.
 The fuel cap of 24000 steps (~6 GB) is past any guard on a 3 GB guest:
 printing WALK COMPLETED means the frontier crossed the page unnoticed,
 which is the failure this arm exists to catch.

Section: Definitions

  grow : Text, Integer -> Text
  grow (t) (k) =
   if k <= 0 then t
   else grow (t & t) (k - 1)

  walk : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  walk (big) (acc) (n) =
   if n <= 0 then acc
   else let t = big & "x"
    in walk big (acc + text-length t) (n - 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let big = grow "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123" 12
   in act
    print-line-uni ("walking: step " & show (text-length big))
    print-line-uni ("burned: " & show (walk big 0 24000))
    print-line-uni "WALK COMPLETED"
   end
  end
